      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a+b?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2b=6a+14 \\\\ 5b+25=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We number the equations so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2b=6a+14 & \\,\\,(1) \\\\ 5b+25=0. & \\,\\,(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $(2),$ we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b+25 & =0 \\\\ 5b & =-25 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-5$ into equation $(1)$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-5) & =6a+14 \\\\ -10 & =6a+14 \\\\ -10-14 & =6a \\\\ 6a & =-24 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=-5.$ So,\n\n$$\na+b=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$",
